/DoNotUploadOnGithub/

# Decrypted key material extracted from the real target device
systembag.kb/keybag_decrypted
dump/systembag_live.kb
dump/systembag.kb.enc
dump/iv_key.txt

# Raw/patched Apple kernelcache and kext binaries — copyrighted Apple firmware,
# only the patch logic (kernel_patch/do_patch.py, patches/*.diff) is published
kernel_patch/kernelcache*.enc
kernel_patch/kernelcache*.pack
kernel_patch/kernelcache*.raw
binaries/kernelcache.release.n42.orig
/IOCryptoAcceleratorFamily.bin

# Stale pre-rename leftover copy of ipwndfu from the project's original
# ~/Code/iHack directory (before the rename to iHack2), superseded by
# /ipwndfu — resolved, see CREDITS.md
/iHack/

# Abandoned tool (SSH Ramdisk_Maker 2.0): macOS-only (hdiutil, xpwntool,
# iBoot32Patcher are Mach-O), never ran on Linux, replaced by Legacy-IOS-Kit's
# own SSH ramdisk. Also bundles real Apple-signed iBSS firmware blobs —
# resolved, see CREDITS.md
/32bit-SSH-Ramdisk-0.2-Brute/

# Loose armv7 build artifacts already covered by submodules/patches:
# device_infos/restored_external are compiled output of
# iphone-dataprotection/ramdisk_tools/{device_infos,restored_external}.c
# (already in that submodule). bruteforce/lzssdec predate this documented
# session with no traceable source — see CREDITS.md
binaries/bruteforce
binaries/device_infos
binaries/restored_external
binaries/lzssdec

# Compiled build artifacts added on top of vendored clones
gaster/gaster
ldid/ldid_linux_x86_64
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Local backup/original files left over from editing
*.orig

# Personal-data-derived wordlists (real names, custom candidate lists)
